Week 2 Progress Report
ELT Pipeline & Initial Data Modeling
Scope
Week 2 covers landing the scraped data into the Lakehouse's Bronze layer, cleaning it into a typed Silver layer,
and establishing the relationships between the internal manufacturing tables that Week 3's fuzzy-matching step
will build on.
Data Engineering — Bronze fi Silver
bronze_to_silver.py (pandas, run locally) performs the cleaning; pyspark_production/02_silver_clean.py is the
PySpark + Delta Lake equivalent for the real cluster. Steps:
• De-duplication on listing_id
• Price parsing: "$1106.36" fi 1106.36 (float)
• Condition-text fi numeric condition factor (e.g. "Used - Good" fi 0.58)
• Seller-rating string fi float percentage
• Listing-type classification: whole laptop vs. spare part, with component keyword extraction (Motherboard /
Display / Battery / Keyboard / RAM / SSD)
• Title noise-stripping to prepare for SKU fuzzy-matching in Week 3
